      <div type="clause" n="67">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 67</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="354" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hwa wylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_67.lnote.oe.1-3"/> georne fram unrihte gecirran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_67.lnote.oe.2-2"/> eft to rihte, miltsige man for Godes ege, swa man best<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_67.lnote.oe.star"/> mæge, þam swyþe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_67.lnote.oe.3-2"/> georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="354" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf hwa wille georne fra<hi rend="italic">m</hi> unrihte to rihte gecyrran, mildsige man him for Godes ege, swa man betst mæge, ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_67.lnote.oe.1"/> men swyðe georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="354" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hwa wille georne fram unrihte gecyrran eft to rihte, miltsige mann for Godes ege, swa man best mage, þam swiðe georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="355" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si aliquis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_67.lnote.oe.1-2"/> uelit ab<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_67.lnote.oe.2"/> iniusticia reuerti ad rectum, remittatur ei pro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_67.lnote.oe.3"/> timore Dei, sicut melius poterit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="67" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="355" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis autem ab iniusticia sua ad iusticiam conuerti uoluerit, misericordia super eum fiat propter timorem Domini, in quantum misericordie racio expostulauerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="67" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="206" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf hwa wille georne fram unrihte to rihte gecyrran<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IICn_67.robnote.fn.10"/>, mildsige man him<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IICn_67.robnote.fn.11"/> for Godes ege, swa man betst mæge<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IICn_67.robnote.fn.12"/>, ðam men swyðe georne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="286" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gif hwa wylle georne fram unrihte gecirran eft to rihte, miltsige man for Godes ege, swa man betst mæge, þam swyþe georne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="355" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn einer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_67.lnote.de.1"/> willig von Unrecht wieder zur Rechtsordnung umkehren will, so erbarme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_67.lnote.de.2"/> man sich aus Gottesfurcht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_67.lnote.de.3"/>, wie man bestens vermag, dessen recht willig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone is willing to turn back from wrong to the order of law, let one take pity, out of fear of God, as best one can, very willingly on him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="207" ed="#robertson"/>If anyone zealously desires to turn from lawlessness to observance of the law, as great mercy as possible shall be shown to him, with the utmost readiness, through the fear of God.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="471" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone eagerly wishes to turn from wrong-doing back to right behaviour, one is to be merciful to him very readily, as best one can, for the fear of God.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="287" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if anyone sincerely desires to turn from lawlessness to justice, as much mercy as possible must be shown to him with very great eagerness, for fear of God.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘best’ was altered to ‘betst’ in G (archaising, Liebermann says).; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 355, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">eft to rihte: omitted B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">man for: man him for B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">betst: best G</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">mæge: B adds, then crosses out, ðam men</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ð. m. <hi rend="italic">unterstrichen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ð. m. underlined</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quis ab i. u. r. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quis ab i. u. r. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">de <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">de Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wille <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wille Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gecyr. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gecyr. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert</hi> betst <hi rend="italic">G</hi> [<hi rend="italic">archaisirend; vgl. Hs. A:</hi> best]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected to betst G [archaizing; cf. MS A: best]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">swiþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">swiþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. 2a; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Barmherzigkeit 2b. c. Ob besonders der dem Gerichte Entwichene in c. 66 gemeint ist, der sich nachträglich nun stellt?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 2a; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Barmherzigkeit 2b. c. Is the man meant in particular the one who has absconded from the court in c. 66 and now afterwards gives himself up?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. 2a; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Barmherzigkeit 2b. c. Ob besonders der dem Gerichte Entwichene in c. 66 gemeint ist, der sich nachträglich nun stellt?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 2a; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Barmherzigkeit 2b. c. Is the man meant in particular the one who has absconded from the court in c. 66 and now afterwards gives himself up?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_67.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Godes ege s</hi>. 68, 1; Einl. 19</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Godes ege see</hi> 68, 1; Introduction 19</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_67.robnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope></bibl><label>gecyrran</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gecirran (-y-) eft to r.</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_67.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope></bibl><label>him</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_67.robnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope></bibl><label>mæge</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">m. ðam men</hi> B, with <hi rend="italic">ð. m.</hi> crossed out.</seg></note>
      </div>
